{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A6D5ncvZpikzVCj1dFqyAQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd100-chroot\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/chroot: Run a Command with a Different Root Directory\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships chroot but the GNU version supports --userspec and --groups flags. The Go\n6\t  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchroot, installed by\n7\t  coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n8\t  via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Change the root directory and run a command in the new root.\n12\t  - G2: Support user and group specification for the chrooted process.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchroot via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Chroot execution\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must call chroot(2) to change the root directory to NEWROOT, then execute COMMAND with any arguments. If no COMMAND is given, must execute ${SHELL} -i (default /bin/sh -i).\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"--userspec=USER:GROUP must set the UID and GID of the executed process. USER and GROUP may be names or numeric IDs.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"--groups=G_LIST must set the supplementary groups of the executed process. G_LIST is a comma-separated list of group names or GIDs.\"\n25\t\n26\t  R2:\n27\t    title: Exit codes\n28\t    items:\n29\t      - R2.1:\n30\t          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n31\t      - R2.2:\n32\t          text: Must exit 125 when chroot itself fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n33\t      - R2.3:\n34\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n35\t\n36\tnon_goals:\n37\t  - cmd/chroot does not set up the chroot filesystem; the caller must prepare NEWROOT.\n38\t  - cmd/chroot does not implement --skip-chdir.\n39\t\n40\tacceptance_criteria:\n41\t  - id: AC1\n42\t    criterion: \"chroot /tmp /bin/echo hello runs echo in a chroot, matching gchroot.\"\n43\t    traces:\n44\t      - R1.1\n45\t  - id: AC2\n46\t    criterion: \"chroot with non-existent root exits 125, matching gchroot.\"\n47\t    traces:\n48\t      - R2.2\n49\t  - id: AC3\n50\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gchroot passes.\"\n51\t    traces:\n52\t      - R1.1\n53\t  - id: AC4\n54\t    criterion: \"cmd/chroot compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n55\t    traces:\n56\t      - R1.1\n57\t      - R1.2\n58\t      - R1.3\n59\t      - R2.1\n60\t      - R2.2\n61\t      - R2.3\n62\t\n63\tpackage_contract:\n64\t  imports:\n65\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dd5dfd7f-8cde-46a9-b2d5-a4f5ecae8459","uuid":"ad2ad9e1-6d5d-448c-b95e-eca8c4de5fb0","timestamp":"2026-05-27T14:49:48.620Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5588/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd100-chroot.yaml","content":"id: srd100-chroot\ntitle: \"cmd/chroot: Run a Command with a Different Root Directory\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships chroot but the GNU version supports --userspec and --groups flags. The Go\n  implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchroot, installed by\n  coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential testing\n  via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Change the root directory and run a command in the new root.\n  - G2: Support user and group specification for the chrooted process.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchroot via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Chroot execution\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must call chroot(2) to change the root directory to NEWROOT, then execute COMMAND with any arguments. If no COMMAND is given, must execute ${SHELL} -i (default /bin/sh -i).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"--userspec=USER:GROUP must set the UID and GID of the executed process. USER and GROUP may be names or numeric IDs.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"--groups=G_LIST must set the supplementary groups of the executed process. G_LIST is a comma-separated list of group names or GIDs.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 125 when chroot itself fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/chroot does not set up the chroot filesystem; the caller must prepare NEWROOT.\n  - cmd/chroot does not implement --skip-chdir.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"chroot /tmp /bin/echo hello runs echo in a chroot, matching gchroot.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"chroot with non-existent root exits 125, matching gchroot.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gchroot passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/chroot compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
